  "notes": "A cube of N*N*N multipliers, one per (i, j, k): the start edge writes every product A[i][k]*B[k][j] into its own register. For each output entry one registered binary adder tree (2N-1 nodes in heap layout, one level per cycle, no enables) sums the N products, and C registers the root in every cycle; a step counter raises done. No operand register moves and no counter selects an operand. Latency clog2(N) + 1 (3 at N = 4). The flat tree vector has N*N*(2N-1)*AccW bits, more than 2^31 at some in-range points.",
  "player": "dicecrane",
